A||||9||87FieroGTx||Brake prob?||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||06-27-2001||04:18 PM|||| I was coming home from work today in my 85 GT I stoped to git a drink and there was white smoke coming from the front right wheel well and it pulls to the right side(<P> Anyone know what's wrong? Could it have locked up?<P> How would I fix it??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-27-2001||04:21 PM||||did your face feel warm when you looked at it? was the wheel hot? dont touch the rotor - your finger might stick to it while it frys.<P>  if its pulling to that side sounds like your caliper has siezed up, or maybe a brake pad has fallen loose and jammed.<P> Or white smoke could be you are loosing brake fluid onto the rotor and its burning off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87FieroGTx||06-27-2001||05:04 PM|||| Now that I look at it I think it is the caliper. <P> How would I go about fixing it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||06-27-2001||06:41 PM||||Is the caliper rubbing on the rim, or is the puck stuck?<BR>If it is rubbing, bolt it back in place...<BR>If the puck is stuck, replace BOTH sides, makes a wonderfull improvement...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||87FieroGTx||06-27-2001||08:13 PM|||| I took it apart! The Piston is stuck, I used a C clamp to compress it then stuck it back on for now but now I have no right front brake but its beter than having it all the way on.<P> How do I fix it? Should I just buy a new one or should I try to rebuild it?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||06-27-2001||09:06 PM||||Mine is doing the same thing... Except it doesn't do it all the time...<P>I'm going to check prices for new calipers but probably just depend on one of my brothers here on the forum to see me good used ones at a good price.... I'm going to go ahead and do both sides too. I like nice even braking...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||acehilton||06-27-2001||09:41 PM||||I rebuilt the brakes on my 86 last summer.  Got the parts at Car Quest, was a reletivly easy job.  <P>My calipers hadn't locked up, but they were leaking all over the place.  The calipers were gunked up, they were starting to get sticky.   After a good cleaning (I think I cornered the market in brake cleaner), and new rotors, braking was considerably improved.<P>The pucks had a little burring going on.  I solved that little problem with 1500 grit sandpaper on both the pucks and the bores (I used solvent to wet sand them).<P>Now, my brakes are as good as new for about a quarter of the price of outright replacemant.<P>The only problem I had was bleeding the stupid things.  A Mity-Vac goes a long way tword solving that problem.<P>I would certinaly try to rebuild first before shelling out for a rebuilt/new caliper.<P>Hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||87FieroGTx||06-28-2001||11:30 AM|||| I just went out and bought new ones I'm going to unstall them tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||06-28-2001||11:50 AM|||| Is there anything I can do to prevent the other brake calipers from seizing?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||06-28-2001||12:03 PM||||the front calipers are not expensive on the pre 88 cars - I think I got a rebuild for less than $25 - $30.<P>  its the rear ones that cost - $90 or so!||||reg||1
